WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:31.170
Hey everybody!

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:35.400
It's almost finale time, I'm beginning to get all kinds of questions about Viserion and the Night King.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.880
So I figured it's time to start talking about endgame theories for them,

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.780
because this is not slowing down at all.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:47.300
There are a couple big questions to answer so we know that this is going into season eight the Night King is making it south of the wall,

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:52.800
but what is he going to do with Viserion aside from just patrol around the army of the dead?

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:59.500
They've lost some of their number, but presumably when they break south of the wall they replenish those and then some exponentially.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:04.760
So when we're talking about killing the Night King and killing Viserion you have to sort of clarify what the rules are like,

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:09.040
what is Viserion now? Is he a white, or is he more like the white walkers?

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:14.320
Because there's a big difference Viserion would still need his tissue otherwise, he couldn't fly.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:20.540
And whites decompose unlike the white walkers. Who seemingly aged, but maybe at a much slower rate.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:25.890
There's a lot of questions about the way white walkers age, because Craster's babies get turned,

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:31.360
but once he touches them and his magic takes hold do they just immediately sprout into Fully-Grown white walkers?

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.980
Or do they age at the same rate that other human beings would?

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:39.740
I think the idea is that his magic takes hold of them and they grow at a much accelerated rate,

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:46.400
but they still decompose because there's only a handful of white walkers that we know of here, but way back during season four

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:51.299
there's all of these standing in the background and Jon has killed a couple himself,

00:01:51.429 --> 00:01:57.958
Samwell killed one. So let's just assume that for hundreds of years people have been offering sacrifices like Craster.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:03.599
There have been white walkers that have grown, died off, and then replenished through new babies that have come along.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.540
But I've gotten so many questions about Viserion now.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:11.460
Because he's been turned by the Night King, will he still grow? So a lot of people saw the blue eye

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:16.979
and they just took that to mean that he was like the white walkers, but whites also have blue eyes.

00:02:16.989 --> 00:02:22.229
So that's not necessarily a confirmation. Right now, just based on the evidence the show has given us,

00:02:22.229 --> 00:02:28.320
I'm treating him like a bigger more complicated version of the white polar bear that we saw earlier in the episode.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:33.120
I think the idea now is that he has all the same abilities that he had before. He breathes fire.

00:02:33.489 --> 00:02:35.489
because if they're gonna take down the wall,

00:02:35.489 --> 00:02:39.240
And he's going to help, it's gonna have to be fire. People are like "Will he breathe frost?"

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:45.540
The really easy conclusion to make there is that frost isn't gonna help bring down a giant ice wall, you're gonna need fire.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:51.299
So wouldn't it be cool if he breathes blue fire, and that's just a function of the Night King's magic.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:56.980
But he can ride him like a normal mount he can send him on patrol so the Night King can just walk around on the ground,

00:02:57.020 --> 00:03:02.180
while Viserion is strafing or doing whatever he wants. He can also use him as a recon tool.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:07.020
So he can see through Vissarion's eyes the way that Bran sees through the eyes of the raven. Now,

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:12.180
they haven't completely defined the Night King's powers. All of his abilities flow through the Children of the Forest.

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:17.820
So anything that they were capable of doing the Night King is probably capable of doing a version of that too.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:23.360
But in turning him into a weapon it sounds like they just imbued him with a bunch of extra abilities on top of that.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:29.960
This nightmare of nature that could raise the dead in control massive armies. He can control all of the whites simultaneously,

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:36.760
and like they said you kill him you kill everyone else because he created them all so this is a really important idea.

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:40.800
Because the big question is, what kind of final battle are we moving towards?

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:45.870
Will they actually make it past Winterfell or is that where the final battle is gonna take place?

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:49.760
And it'll just be over a couple of episodes, like it'll all just happen up there.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:55.500
Because if they make it past Winterfell, it'll probably be because they've washed over it like a biblical plague

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.940
So think about how heartbreaking it was when the Bolton's took Winterfell.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:03.260
If the army of the dead were to take Winterfell, that would almost be too much.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:08.140
But if they don't make it south, then Battle of Gondor style, like your final battle takes place there.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:11.620
Even though the Gondor of Game of Thrones is down in King's Landing,

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:15.860
It would be a nice way to sort of deflect for the battle for the Iron Throne

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:22.000
Everybody says that it doesn't matter well if the final battle takes place at winterfell, then it really wouldn't matter.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:26.440
And pretty soon we're probably gonna have all of our important characters up in the north anyway.

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:29.480
Because they're either going to Winterfell or going to the wall.

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:33.540
So you have this whole idea that there's not gonna be anything interesting happening in the south

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:39.060
So it paints a very different picture than what I think people's expectations were when the series first started.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.520
Because King's landing has been the center of everything.

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:45.400
Way back in season four we saw the shadow of a dragon flying over it,

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:49.920
That was a vision that Bran had had that might have been a vision of the future with Daenerys

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:54.500
flying over King's landing on Drogon because we haven't seen her in any of the promos.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:05:00.860
And I think that's just to maintain some surprise because when she at this big meeting that they're having she'll arrive on dragon back

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:03.560
So there will be a dragon over King's Landing.

00:05:03.980 --> 00:05:08.000
But in the way that the series sold Ned Stark as the protagonist during season one.

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:10.950
I also think it's a misdirect with King's Landing and the Iron Throne.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:15.630
Daenerys had all those visions of it in ruins with snow falling on the ground.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:21.869
You could take that as a vision of the future the Night King bringing Viserion to King's Landing and just destroying everything.

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:27.180
But after the fact, as the visions are sort of explained to Daenerys, there are things that might have happened.

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:32.429
Or it could have happened had things been different, so I think this isn't meant to be a literal future.

00:05:32.429 --> 00:05:34.560
I think it's meant to be a combination of futures.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:43.220
Maybe Daenerys with her dragons didn't listen to Tyrion, destroys everything, and then winter eventually comes, because they did not come together.

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:46.420
So whether he makes it that far south or whether they hold him at Winterfell,

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:49.820
they need to kill the Night King and they need to kill Viserion.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:55.180
There was one really big way for killing a dragon whether he was undead or not, earlier this season.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:06:00.120
There's the giant Scorpion that Bronn took Drogon down with. They'll have to use that,

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:05.640
but I think that they'll also have to add some Dragon Glass or maybe even to make a Valyrian steel bolt

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:07.800
The characters haven't learned how to do that yet,

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:14.800
But Gendry, "Master Blacksmith" could borrow or take somebody's Valyrian sword melt that down and turn it into a Valyrian steel bolt.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:21.060
I think it would be a little disingenuous if there wasn't at least a little bit of a big "Battle of the Bastards" situation.

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:25.880
Where you actually have a big pitched battle army of the dead versus the united forces of the south.

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:30.840
But really you need to get someone in close to the Night King, so that requires a dragon,

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:32.320
and someone who's really agile.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:37.460
So, a lot of Arya Stark theories flying around, but you could either drop her from one of the other dragons

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:42.380
But if you're unable to bring Viserion down and the Night King remains on his back, out of reach,

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:48.360
You could try to use one of the dragons to airlift her in and get her close with her dagger, whether or not that be effective.

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:52.020
We've never actually seen someone fight the Night King in close combat.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:57.520
So you have to imagine that as badass as the white walkers are the Night King is an extra level above that.

00:06:57.880 --> 00:07:02.400
The smarter way would probably be to take Viserion down with a Scorpion bolt,

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:07.660
then get someone in close to the Night King, because if you killed the Night King while they were flying in the air,

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:15.000
per the rules Viserion would die immediately and then who ever went in to kill the Night King would just freefall until somebody picked him up.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:18.440
So you guys can let me know in the comments, which method do you prefer?

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:20.020
Someone is gonna have to kill the Night King.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:23.840
I mean, It will definitely be someone who gets in close and ganks him and takes down

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:28.380
most of the army that hasn't already been killed by the united forces of the south.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:36.040
But, do you prefer someone do that while they're flying through the air or after they've already killed Viserion using one of the Scorpions?

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:40.760
But as sort of a tangent to that, people are wondering what's gonna happen with Rhaegal and Drogon.

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:47.000
So you have two on one now. They'll have to at least attempt some sort of aerial spit-fire battle with all three of them.

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:54.740
But I really do feel like Drogon and Rhaegal will make it out of this, or at least in time to lay new dragon eggs and fertilize them.

00:07:54.969 --> 00:07:59.458
Daenerys has been barren for all this time. She believes that she's not going to have any more children.

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:01.760
She believes there won't be any more dragons.

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:06.180
So I think the big surprise is that she will eventually get pregnant again and have a child,

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:11.280
and sort of flowing from that, new dragons will also be born, or at least dragon eggs will be laid.

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:15.600
We really don't know how long it takes for them to gestate that could be multiple lifetimes.

00:08:15.669 --> 00:08:19.708
So the characters on the show now might be dead before more dragons are born.

00:08:19.869 --> 00:08:24.479
In per Maester Aemon in the books we find out the dragons are sort of asexual.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:29.640
They're neither male nor female, so whether or not they choose to do that, it is possible for them to mate.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:33.760
But let me know what's all your Night King/Viserion theories in the comments below

00:08:34.060 --> 00:08:36.640
But because we've been talking a lot about Daenerys being childless.

